      </div>
      <div>
        <p><strong>Q: Does RackNerd offer a money-back guarantee?</strong></p>
        <p>A: RackNerd has a 30-day refund policy for new accounts, subject to terms and conditions.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p><strong>Q: Which RackNerd datacenter should I choose?</strong></p>
        <p>A: For Asia-Pacific access, Los Angeles (LA) offers the best latency. For US East Coast, New York or Chicago are optimal.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Conclusion</h2>
      <p>RackNerd is the undisputed king of budget VPS in 2025. With prices starting at $1.99/month, no other provider comes close on price-to-performance. Best for developers, hobbyists, and anyone needing affordable US-based VPS hosting.</p>
      <p>The lack of NVMe storage is the main trade-off — if you need fast disk I/O for production AI workloads, Vultr's NVMe-equipped plans at $24/month are worth the premium. But for pure value per dollar, RackNerd is untouchable.</p>

